1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,073
One equation sums up cellular respiration.

2
00:00:03,323 --> 00:00:04,561
Here's how to read it.

3
00:00:05,011 --> 00:00:09,896
Glucose plus 6 O2 gives 6 CO2, 6 H2O, and energy.

4
00:00:10,346 --> 00:00:12,138
Cells use it to make ATP.

5
00:00:12,388 --> 00:00:16,271
Eukaryotes get roughly 30 to 32 ATP per glucose.

6
00:00:16,721 --> 00:00:21,521
And all 6 CO2 molecules are released along the way, per glucose.

